  "text": {
    "intro": "The Hollow Creek county fair runs its pie judging with more ceremony than the state legislature.\nFive bakers are involved. Determine each baker's placing, filling and crust.\n- **Baker**: Odette, Bramwell, Thaddeus, Caspian and Marigold.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third, fourth and fifth.\n- **Filling**: blackberry, green tomato, mincemeat, pecan and rhubarb.\n- **Crust**: a braided edge, a double crust, a fork-crimped edge, a crumb topping and a lattice top.\nEvery baker has a different placing, filling and crust, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Second is exactly one place better than Bramwell, with no placing in between. Bramwell uses a braided edge.",
      "Caspian places first.",
      "The baker who uses a double crust falls somewhere between fifth and first in placing order.",
      "The baker who uses a crumb topping is worse than third in placing order. The baker who bakes rhubarb and third are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Marigold is better than third in placing order.",
      "The baker who uses a fork-crimped edge is better than the baker who bakes mincemeat in placing order. Odette and the baker who bakes mincemeat are exactly two places apart in placing order.",
      "Caspian and the baker who bakes blackberry are exactly two places apart in placing order.",
      "The baker who uses a crumb topping falls somewhere between the baker who bakes blackberry and the baker who bakes pecan in placing order."
    ]
